96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 38 0 R
/K [830 0 R 831 0 R 832 0 R 833 0 R 834 0 R 835 0 R 836 0 R]
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Alt (Flowchart detailing participant enrollment and allocation in a study. Initially, 100 individuals were assessed; 33 were excluded. Randomization divided 77 participants into three groups: MPT \(25\), HPT \(25\), and CTR \(27\). During follow-up, interventions were discontinued for some: MPT \(1\), HPT \(2\), CTR \(5\) due to reasons like high-intensity activity outside the study or lack of tests. In the analysis phase, the groups included MPT \(24\), HPT \(23\), and CTR \(22\).)
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 38 0 R
/K [837 0 R 838 0 R 839 0 R 840 0 R 841 0 R 842 0 R 843 0 R]
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Alt (Study design infographic for a training program involving 77 male basketball players. After two weeks of familiarization, participants are randomized into three groups: Micro-Plyometric Jump Training \(MRT\) with 400 repetitions weekly, Macro-Plyometric Jump Training \(HRT\) with 800 repetitions, and a control group. Training is done in supervised sessions, four times weekly, at a constant intensity and time. A four-week intervention is conducted, followed by post-testing. Testing includes various physical assessments like sprints and aerobic endurance. The program progresses from a basic to an advanced period over four weeks.)
>>
endobj
