/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Alt (Six violin plots display pre- and post-measurements across different variables: Countermovement Jump, Countermovement Jump-A, Drop Jump, Reaction Strength Index, Modified Reaction Strength Index, and Maximum Strength. Significant differences are indicated with asterisks. Groups are color-coded: MPT 400 \(pink\), HPT 800 \(purple\), and CTR \(blue\).)
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 38 0 R
/K [851 0 R 852 0 R 853 0 R 854 0 R 855 0 R 856 0 R 857 0 R]
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Alt (Six graphs display pre and post-test results for three groups: MPT 400, HPT 800, and CTR, in pink, purple, and blue, respectively. The metrics include: 0-10m, 0-20m, 10-20m sprint times, T agility test, 5-0-5 agility test, and maximal oxygen uptake. Significant differences are indicated with asterisks. Each group shows performance improvements post-test. The violin plots illustrate data distribution and mean differences for each group.)
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 38 0 R
/K [858 0 R 859 0 R 860 0 R 861 0 R 862 0 R 863 0 R 864 0 R]
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Alt (Six violin plots display IMTP \(Isometric Mid-Thigh Pull\) force data at various milliseconds: 50, 100, 150, 200, 250, and 300. Each plot shows pre- and post-intervention results for three groups: MPT 400 \(pink\), HPT 800 \(purple\), and CTR \(blue\). Black dots indicate means, and lines connect pre- and post-measurements. Asterisks and lines above each plot indicate significant differences.)
>>
